1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,420
I survived one hundred days in hardcore Minecraft.

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:05,640
One life. No second chances.

3
00:00:06,500 --> 00:00:09,530
And on day eighty-seven... I fought the Ender Dragon.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,200
This is what happened.

5
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:21,720
Day one. I spawned in the middle of a plains biome, with absolutely nothing.

6
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:26,050
So I did what every player does first. I punched a tree.

7
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,400
Logs became planks. Planks became a crafting table.

8
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,800
And then, my very first wooden pickaxe.

9
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:43,390
But the sun was already going down. And in hardcore, the first night can end everything.

10
00:00:50,600 --> 00:00:54,340
I threw together a tiny dirt hut, and sealed myself inside.

11
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:58,190
Then the zombies came. One... two... three of them.

12
00:01:01,600 --> 00:01:04,950
I just stood there, holding my only torch, waiting for the sun.

13
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:08,970
Not my proudest moment...

14
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:14,110
but at sunrise, the zombies burned, and I survived night one.

15
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,230
Day two. It was time for a real home.

16
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:28,410
I chopped half a forest, crafted stacks of planks, and started building.

17
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:33,930
Oak logs in the corners. Glass windows. A flat roof.

18
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:41,500
And on day six, my first real house was done.

19
00:01:48,900 --> 00:01:52,520
Day eight. I stayed out too late, and three zombies cornered me.

20
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:55,470
Good thing I'd just crafted an iron sword.

21
00:01:59,900 --> 00:02:01,410
Three zombies. Three hits.

22
00:02:03,700 --> 00:02:09,660
In hardcore, every fight is life or death. So from now on, I never leave home without a sword.

23
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,520
By day twelve, my food was running low, so I built a farm.

24
00:02:22,600 --> 00:02:25,620
Water in the middle, and wheat planted on every side.

25
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:29,500
A few days later... my first harvest.

26
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:35,370
Then I used that wheat to lead some cows and sheep home, and fenced them in.

27
00:02:38,600 --> 00:02:41,820
By day fifteen, I had bread, steak, and wool for a bed.

28
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:45,350
Now I could finally skip the nights.

29
00:02:50,600 --> 00:02:53,420
Day nineteen. I was chopping wood when I heard it.

30
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:54,700
That hiss.

31
00:02:58,600 --> 00:03:02,360
Here it is in slow motion. I backed off at the very last second.

32
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:11,630
One more step, and this would have been a very short video.

33
00:03:18,900 --> 00:03:23,770
Days twenty-three to thirty, I went deep. Branch mining, one tunnel at a time.

34
00:03:24,900 --> 00:03:26,010
And then... I saw it.

35
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:28,220
Diamonds!

36
00:03:32,100 --> 00:03:34,230
One vein. Then another. Then another.

37
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:43,430
Nine diamonds. Enough for a pickaxe, a sword, and armor.

38
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:51,750
Day thirty-four. I came home from the mine, and there was a creeper next to my house.

39
00:03:52,600 --> 00:03:53,550
I couldn't stop it.

40
00:03:56,600 --> 00:03:59,910
Thirty-four days of work... and half my house was gone.

41
00:04:05,600 --> 00:04:09,460
So I rebuilt it, and put torches on every single block around it.

42
00:04:15,900 --> 00:04:20,840
Day forty-one. I didn't want to waste diamonds mining obsidian, so I used a trick.

43
00:04:21,300 --> 00:04:25,430
Lava into a dirt mold, then water on top. One block at a time.

44
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:28,700
Ten obsidian, flint and steel...

45
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:32,330
and I was going to the Nether.

46
00:04:44,600 --> 00:04:49,270
The Nether is huge and deadly, so on day forty-five, I built an ice highway.

47
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,070
Blue ice, a boat, and glass walls on both sides.

48
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:58,490
Seventy-two blocks per second. Nothing in the Nether could catch me.

49
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:16,220
Day fifty-two. I needed netherite, the best gear in the game.

50
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:20,750
Beds explode in the Nether, so I used one to blow up the wall.

51
00:05:23,100 --> 00:05:24,070
Watch it again.

52
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:34,300
Three ancient debris, from one blast.

53
00:05:40,800 --> 00:05:45,330
Day sixty almost ended everything. I was bridging to a sky island...

54
00:05:45,480 --> 00:05:46,330
and I slipped.

55
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:55,890
In hardcore, that's game over. Unless you have a water bucket.

56
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,610
One click before the ground, and I lived.

57
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:13,950
Day seventy-four. In a trial chamber, I found the strongest weapon in the game.

58
00:06:14,100 --> 00:06:15,740
The mace. Wind charge up...

59
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:19,400
fall down... smash.

60
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:25,130
The higher you fall, the harder it hits.

61
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:43,650
Day eighty. Diamond gear, golden apples, and a stack of arrows. I was ready.

62
00:06:44,600 --> 00:06:48,750
I followed my eyes of ender to a stronghold, and filled the portal frame.

63
00:06:54,400 --> 00:06:56,280
Twelve eyes. The portal was open.

64
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:01,100
There was no turning back now.

65
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:10,770
Day eighty-seven. The End.

66
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:17,010
The Ender Dragon was circling the island, and the crystals on the pillars kept healing it.

67
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:23,420
So first, the crystals. One arrow at a time.

68
00:07:36,600 --> 00:07:38,100
Then the dragon came for me.

69
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:47,290
It landed on the portal, and that was my chance.

70
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,890
Every hit counted. One mistake, and it was over.

71
00:08:02,400 --> 00:08:03,230
Last hit...

72
00:08:07,600 --> 00:08:10,970
The Ender Dragon was dead! I beat the game, in hardcore.

73
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,120
Day ninety-three. In an End city, I found elytra.

74
00:08:24,200 --> 00:08:25,550
Finally, I could fly.

75
00:08:28,400 --> 00:08:32,420
I built eight rings across my world, and flew through every single one.

76
00:08:48,100 --> 00:08:50,490
Day ninety-seven. One last challenge.

77
00:08:51,100 --> 00:08:53,780
Jump off a fifty-five block tower, with a mace.

78
00:08:58,100 --> 00:08:59,440
Here it is, slowed down.

79
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:08,080
Fifty-five blocks. One hit.

80
00:09:18,400 --> 00:09:19,440
Day one hundred.

81
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:24,800
From a dirt hut, to a full base, a farm, the Nether, and the Ender Dragon.

82
00:09:27,600 --> 00:09:30,380
One hundred days. One life. And I never died.

83
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:37,230
Should I do two hundred days? Tell me in the comments.

84
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:42,350
And subscribe to HollowCraft, so you don't miss it.

